  "metadata": {
    "title": "A fixed moment separator without a rational normalized sum-of-squares certificate",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23196750",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-06",
    "description": "<p>This research note exhibits the phenomenon asked about in the literal fixed-polynomial certificate question in Oberwolfach Report 14/2023, under an explicit rational polynomial-square convention. On the rational unit ball in three variables, p=1+f for Scheiderer's classical quartic has minimum one and annihilates an explicit rational degree-four moment vector of mass one. It belongs to 1+Q_R(g) but not to 1+Q_Q(g), even with arbitrary finite multiplier degrees. The input moment matrix is not positive semidefinite. A different polynomial q=1+x^4 certifies the same vector rationally, p itself is rationally positivity-certifiable, and every rational rescaling cp with c&gt;1 has a rational normalized certificate. The result is outside the companion preprint's strict-margin regime and asserts no algorithm, minimal degree or general descent theorem.</p><p>The contribution is an explicit normalized-moment application and scope clarification of established ingredients. Scheiderer's quartic and field obstruction, the classical leading-form/completion mechanism, Benoist's formal-ring observation, Nie's earlier ball application, the prior irrational Gram and Naldi-Sinn semidefinite-infeasibility applications, and Powers' strictly positive rational certificate are credited. The portable archive supplies the manuscript source, all 35 exact rational moments and sparse polynomial data, a Python-standard-library checker with its complete byte-identical expected 2,059-check output, claim and priority notes, publication metadata, source-version provenance and a file-hash manifest. Finite computations supplement the written Galois and all-degree local proofs; they are not finite-search proofs of arbitrary-degree impossibility.</p><p>Three independently initiated bounded priority families identified no exact earlier normalized-moment application in the primary passages inspected. Their actual reading extents, unavailable or unexamined final and duplicate bodies, and the unknown remainder and Appendix B.1 statement of the differing 2026 corrected descent proof are disclosed. No worldwide-firstness, current-openness or originating-author-intent guarantee is claimed. AI tools were used extensively in developing the application, literature comparison, exact computations, writing and adversarial checking. This is an unrefereed preprint without independent human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification.</p>",
